{"name":"Sweetheart","hex":"#f3c3d8","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweetheart","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is always very kind.","A person very much liked or loved by someone, especially when both partners are young."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweetheart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweetheart Abbey","blocks":[{"text":"The Abbey of Dulce Cor, better known as Sweetheart Abbey, was a Cistercian monastery founded in 1273 in what is now the village of New Abbey, in the historical county of Kirkcudbrightshire in Dumfries and Galloway, 8 miles (13 km) south of Dumfries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Sweetheart_Abbey.jpg/330px-Sweetheart_Abbey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetheart_Abbey"},{"title":"Sweetheart (2019 American film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sweetheart is a 2019 American survival horror film directed by J. D. Dillard, written by Dillard, Alex Theurer and Alex Hyner, and starring Kiersey Clemons, Emory Cohen, Hanna Mangan-Lawrence and Andrew Crawford. It was produced by Jason Blum, Dillard, Theurer, Hyner and Bill Karesh. The movie tells the story of a castaway who washes up on an island and must survive there while being stalked by a humanoid sea monster."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1d/Sweetheart_%282019%29_Film_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetheart_(2019_American_film)"},{"title":"Sweetheart (Rainy Davis song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sweetheart\" is a song originally recorded by American singer Rainy Davis. It was written by Davis and Pete Warner, and produced with Dorothy Kessler. The track was released in 1986 by independent record label SuperTronics as a single from Davis's 1987 studio album Sweetheart. A freestyle, hip hop pop, and synth-funk song, \"Sweetheart\" appeared on R&B and dance music-based record charts in the United States."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetheart_(Rainy_Davis_song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Sweetheart_Abbey.jpg/330px-Sweetheart_Abbey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Sweetheart_Abbey.jpg/330px-Sweetheart_Abbey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASweetheart_Abbey.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Sweetheart_Abbey1.jpg/500px-Sweetheart_Abbey1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Sweetheart_Abbey1.jpg/500px-Sweetheart_Abbey1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Looking eastwards, the impressive nave of the abbey church leading (under the dramatic bell tower) to the chancel, with its richly carved and traceried windows. Above the rows of pillars, the triforia can just be seen.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASweetheart_Abbey1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Sweetheart_Abbey_entrance.jpg/500px-Sweetheart_Abbey_entrance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Sweetheart_Abbey_entrance.jpg/500px-Sweetheart_Abbey_entrance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sweetheart Abbey entrance through the much altered archway in the abbey precincts which extended to 30 acres.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASweetheart_Abbey_entrance.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1d/Sweetheart_%282019%29_Film_Poster.jp